AMMOcoin v1.1.1 for Debian / Ubuntu
====================================

Requirements: Ubuntu 22.04+ or Debian 12+ (glibc 2.34 or newer), amd64 or arm64.
v1.1.1 is the Proof-of-Stake hard fork release; older nodes are on a dead chain.

What the package installs
-------------------------
  /usr/bin/ammocoind               the node (headless; the GUI wallet is the -Qt.AppImage / -Qt.tar.gz release download)
  /usr/bin/ammocoin-cli            RPC client
  /usr/bin/ammocoin-tx             offline transaction tool
  /usr/bin/ammocoin-node-cli       ammocoin-cli for the packaged service (runs as user "ammocoin")
  /usr/bin/ammocoin-fetch-params   installs/verifies the Sapling parameters
  /usr/share/ammocoin/*.params     Sapling parameters (SHA-256 verified at build time)
  /lib/systemd/system/ammocoind.service

The node service
----------------
On first install the package creates the system user "ammocoin" (HOME /var/lib/ammocoin),
writes /var/lib/ammocoin/.ammocoin11/ammocoin.conf (mode 600, random rpcpassword, P2P
port 37020, RPC 51473 on 127.0.0.1, staking=1) and enables + starts ammocoind. An existing
ammocoin.conf is never overwritten. This is the same layout scripts/deployment/install-node.sh
uses, so either can manage the same node.

  systemctl status ammocoind
  journalctl -u ammocoind -f
  ammocoin-node-cli getblockcount
  ammocoin-node-cli getstakingstatus
  sudo systemctl disable --now ammocoind      # if you only wanted the command-line tools

Open TCP 37020 in your firewall for inbound peers. Masternode / cold-staking options go in
ammocoin.conf (see /usr/share/doc/ammocoin/examples/ammocoin.conf), then
`sudo systemctl restart ammocoind`.

Running the node as your own user
---------------------------------
`ammocoind -daemon` as a normal user keeps data in ~/.ammocoin11 and finds the packaged
Sapling parameters in /usr/share/ammocoin automatically. Stop the service first
(`sudo systemctl disable --now ammocoind`), or give your node another -port/-rpcport.
`ammocoin-fetch-params` copies the parameters into ~/.ammocoin-params if you prefer a
per-user copy (or downloads them from download.z.cash when no local copy exists).

Removing
--------
`apt remove ammocoin` stops the service. `apt purge ammocoin` keeps /var/lib/ammocoin and the
"ammocoin" user so wallets are never deleted; back up wallet.dat, then
`sudo deluser --remove-home ammocoin`.
